<BaseLayout title="Maintenance">
  <h1>Maintenance</h1>
  <p>This section brings together scheduled servicing, fluid specifications, tire and wheel care, owner inspections, and service records for the 2021 S60 range. Use the VIN-specific maintenance plan and in-car service reminder as the authority for an individual vehicle.</p>
  <h2>Maintenance topics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="./service-schedule/">Service schedule</a> — routine mileage/time milestones and applicability limits.</li>
    <li><a href="./fluids/">Fluids and capacities</a> — oil, coolant, brake fluid, transmission fluid and washer fluid.</li>
    <li><a href="./oil-level/">Checking engine oil level</a> — electronic oil-level measurement sequence.</li>
    <li><a href="./tires-wheels/">Tires and wheels</a> — placard pressures, fitment, wear, rotation and wheel work.</li>
    <li><a href="./owner-checks/">Owner maintenance checks</a> — periodic inspections between scheduled services.</li>
    <li><a href="./log/">Maintenance and repair log</a> — printable vehicle record and service-entry template.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Powertrain differences matter</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>T5 and T6 gasoline:</strong> use the non-hybrid service schedule only where the published document matches the engine, market and VIN.</li>
    <li><strong>T8 Recharge:</strong> plug-in hybrid maintenance includes high-voltage components and a different maintenance context. Do not apply a non-hybrid schedule wholesale.</li>
    <li><strong>FWD versus AWD:</strong> drivetrain components and service requirements differ. T8's electric rear axle is not serviced like the mechanical AWD hardware on T5/T6.</li>
    <li><strong>Brakes, wheels and options:</strong> brake package, tire sizes, wheel fitment and service parts can vary independently of trim.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Keep a useful service history</h2>
  <p>For every visit, record date, odometer, work performed, exact part numbers, fluid brand and specification, quantity, invoice, warning codes and the next due point. Keep receipts and scan reports with the vehicle record.</p>
  <div class="note"><strong>Do not guess capacities or intervals.</strong> Confirm the exact engine/transmission code and the applicable market-specific Volvo schedule. If a warning message conflicts with a generic interval, follow the vehicle's instruction and obtain qualified diagnosis.</div>
  <h2>2026 cost guide — typical U.S. shop pricing</h2>
  <p>Use these as budgeting ranges for a 2021 S60, not quotes. Prices generally include parts and labor where stated; dealer pricing, brake package, engine, AWD hardware, region and tax can move the total. T8-specific work can cost more and is not fully represented here.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Estimated cost (USD)</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Oil and filter service</th><td>$160–$205</td><td>2021 S60 estimate; synthetic oil and filter.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Cabin air filter</th><td>$125–$175</td><td>Shop replacement estimate.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Brake-fluid service</th><td>$150–$250</td><td>Planning range; confirm fluid spec and whether bleeding is included.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Spark plugs</th><td>$300–$475</td><td>Engine-specific parts and labor; due interval depends on factory schedule.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Timing belt service</th><td>$735–$1,000</td><td>2021 S60 estimate for belt replacement; related tensioners/idlers or water pump may add cost.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Four-wheel alignment</th><td>$145–$215</td><td>Alignment only; worn suspension parts are extra.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
